From eb4be4a50c8959068bf1aa9bf531ed2fd32836f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:57:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, editor: code blocks and quotes in the composer look
 like blocks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.12 (ask 11). The composer is a Markdown buffer, so
fences and `>` quotes were already highlighted while typing (upstream);
they now also read as blocks, and a fence closes itself.

- Every row of a ``` fenced block (fences included; an unclosed fence
  runs to the end, as CommonMark reads it) and every run of quote lines
  gets a background and a 2 px left stripe, from theme colours. The
  rows are recomputed from the text on each Edited event
  (composer_blocks::scan_composer_blocks, a pure function).
- Typing ``` on a line of its own, outside a block, inserts the closing
  fence below and leaves the cursor after the opening one, where a
  language goes. It is its own undo step (finalize_last_transaction on
  both sides), so one undo takes the closing fence back and keeps what
  was typed. A fence that closes an open block is left alone, and so is
  anything after the backticks. It hooks EditorEvent::InputHandled,
  which only the platform input path emits: typed text, never a paste.

The editor part is small and additive: a per-type left border for row
highlights (Editor::set_row_highlight_left_border), carried by
LineHighlight.left_border and painted beside the row background. Kept
per highlight type so highlight_rows and its callers are untouched.

Tests: composer_blocks::tests, 6 unit (scan, fence_to_close) and 3 on
a real MessageEditor (fence closing + undo, a closing fence left alone,
block rows and their stripe, cleared when the text goes). Red seen with
the module registered but not wired: the 3 editor tests failed on the
missing highlight and the missing closing fence.
